From: logos-node-android
Subject: [PATCH 0002] The HTTP API on a Unix socket instead of TCP, when asked for

Against logos-blockchain/logos-blockchain tag 0.3.4 (commit
f7ab0323346d36840660908be049d5a62c905516). Applied with `git apply -p1` by
native/apply-patches.sh. See native/patches/README.md.

On Android any installed app may connect to 127.0.0.1, so the node API's
wallet endpoints (transfer-funds, sign, channel deposit) answer every app on
the phone. With LOGOS_API_UNIX_SOCKET=<path> set for the node process, the
API listens on that socket file and on no TCP port. The value must be an
absolute path in a directory owned by the node's user with no group or other
access; the socket is created under umask 077 and set to 0600; a socket left
by an earlier run is removed only if nothing answers on it. If the variable
is set but anything about the socket is wrong (empty, relative, a shared
directory, a live socket, any other file there, a bind error), the node
stops instead of opening TCP. Unset: upstream behaviour. Routes, handlers,
wallet logic, config format and wire format are unchanged. Independent of
patch 0001.

